{"id": "EUVD-2026-100482", "enisaUuid": "49e73cf2-ece5-38da-866d-4399835b4365", "description": "When a username for an Active Directory connection is a domain without a local part, the auth0-lock library initiates the authentication transaction with a GET request instead of a POST request. As a result, user-submitted form data is appended to the URL as query string parameters.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T20:08:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T18:41:04", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N", "references": ["https://trust.okta.com/security-advisories/improper-request-handling-for-active-directory-logins-in-auth0-lock-cve-2026-107370", "https://github.com/auth0/lock/security/advisories/GHSA-mp8m-wcxp-w648"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-107370"], "assigner": "Okta", "epss": 0.28, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "64c5c92b-924f-333c-91bd-60713668eaea", "product": {"name": "auth0-lock", "vendor": {"name": "auth0"}}, "product_version": "14.0.0 <15.0.2"}, {"id": "c66ff994-0cc6-3da2-b6aa-f672f32074dd", "product": {"name": "auth0-lock", "vendor": {"name": "auth0"}}, "product_version": "10.9.0 <13.2.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "16c2a533-08e6-3d12-be1c-a2da9b89ec60", "vendor": {"name": "auth0"}}], "isExploited": false}